+No actual overlap yet; no production changes. P21 true-residual BLR3e-10 base.
+First small screen retained: 10/20 valid; all 10 reduced-thread attempts failed
+INFO=-58 because MUMPS L0 solve threads must match analysis/factorization.
+This is a terminal library error, not timeout. Do not bypass MUMPS validation.
+
+Revised screen retains MUMPS worker count, caps all process threads to 2 or 4
+physical CPUs during Lanczos, sets outer OMP threads to 2/4, and restores all
+saved CPU masks and outer thread count at scope exit (also on failure).
+The binding splits future overlap resources within 16 physical CPUs:
+main4 on 8,9,16,17 + counters6 on 10-15 and18-23; main2 on8,16 + counters7
+on9-15 and17-23. Main factor still gets16. All configs set OMP_WAIT_POLICY=PASSIVE
+and GOMP_SPINCOUNT=0; do not compare their timing across earlier batches.
+All actual counts still run AFTER main iteration. Observer does not change stop
+or acceptance, only records Ritz values/times. Cost overlap estimates are models,
+not measured end-to-end improvements. Failed first screen remains archived.
+
+Source inspection found a SUPPORTED alternative: MUMPS dini_defaults.F lines734-747 explicitly allows ICNTL(48) switching between factorization and solve. dsol_driver.F lines753-765 reads it each solve and lines2889-2918 requires fixed threads only for L0-on solves. A separate l0_shim prototype is prepared to disable tree parallelism only for JOB3, then reduce ICNTL16, restoring both afterwards. It has not yet been built/run; wait for current dual-core measurement to finish.
